## What We Are Building

SandyStudio is an AI-first animation production studio. This session spanned three distinct chapters:

1. **q1 STITCH per-shot trim** — ffmpeg concat demuxer `outpoint` directive so each per-shot mp4 is trimmed to the animatic-intended duration. Closes the E20 final-cut bug where the cut played 96s (sum of Veo clip native lengths 4s/8s) instead of 54s (sum of `animatic_v1.shot_list[i].duration_seconds`).

2. **Phase 1 fal.ai Seedance 2.0 probe** — standalone CLI exploration of fal.ai Seedance 2.0 image-to-video as an alternative to Veo 3.1. Director tested two motion intents: (a) slow orbit-left revealing more of the perfume counter bar location, (b) Madame + Sandy dancing partner-grip with 360° camera orbit. Both produced fantastic results. Director approved full production integration.

3. **Phase 2 production integration** — wired Seedance 2.0 as a real `MultiVideoGenProvider` end-to-end: provider impl, router registration, type widening, runner refactor, regenerate-video route + single-shot route + Inngest event thread-through, VGENShotPanel + EpisodeTimelineSection UI dropdowns, provider-catalog entries, migration 0028 (default flipped to Seedance for `character_video` contract), 11 unit tests. tsc clean · vitest 198/198 · replay-pilot 29/29. Real probe verified.

4. **Sprint α→ε plan locked** — Director approved next sprint: P0 (Flux 422 fix + E20 archive) → α (Postgres trigger Realtime + team-chat) → β (seedance prompting skill) → γ (E21 production via chat only, zero webapp clicks, live PA-gap audit) → δ (Character Identity Model) → ε (Skill Editor / Learning Loop). Checkpoint memo + PLAN.md rotated.

