## What Did NOT Work (and why)

- **Veo 3.1 Fast & Standard probes for orbit-left img2vid** — failed because: 429 RESOURCE_EXHAUSTED daily quota on both Fast and Standard model buckets. The 25-30 requests fired during E20 SC11 retries earlier that day burned Tier-1 daily quota. $0 spent (429 not billed). Director chose to pivot to fal.ai instead of waiting for ~13h quota reset.
- **Initial fal.ai probe with `fal-ai/bytedance/seedance-2.0/fast/image-to-video` slug (with `fal-ai/` prefix)** — failed because: fal's gateway accepted submit but routed under `fal-ai/bytedance/` parent and returned a stub completion in 0.03s with `"logs": null`, `inference_time: 0.03`. The model didn't actually run. Slug must be without `fal-ai/` prefix: `bytedance/seedance-2.0/fast/image-to-video`.
- **Attempt to use full-slug consistency in status/result URLs (matching Python `fal_client` SDK example)** — failed because: fal's REST gateway truncates `/image-to-video` from status_url/response_url for Seedance 2.0; constructing `https://queue.fal.run/<full-slug>/requests/<id>/status` returns 405 Method Not Allowed. The Python SDK hides this internally. Raw REST must use fal-returned URLs verbatim.
- **First Seedance 2.0 result fetch via fal-returned response_url** — failed because: fal's response_url was parent-truncated to `https://queue.fal.run/fal-ai/bytedance/requests/...` (because we'd submitted with the wrong `fal-ai/` prefix); GET returned 404 `"Path /seedance-2.0/fast/image-to-video not found"`. Fixed by dropping the prefix at submit time so fal's internal routing constructed correct truncated URLs.
- **fal.ai balance exhausted on first real submit** — failed because: 403 `"User is locked. Reason: Exhausted balance"`. Director's fal.ai signup default credit (if any) was zero. Resolved by Director top-up.
- **3 unit tests in fal-seedance.test.ts initial run** — failed because: mock fetch branch matched on `!u.includes('/requests/')` covered BOTH the queue submit URL AND the final video CDN download URL (`https://x/v.mp4`). The CDN GET (no body) overwrote captured submit body to `{}`. Fixed by tightening branch to `u.startsWith('https://queue.fal.run/') && !u.includes('/requests/')`.
- **tsc rejected `Promise<ArrayBufferLike>` in test helper** — failed because: lib.dom union of `ArrayBuffer | SharedArrayBuffer` when `bytes.buffer` accessed. Fixed by copying into plain `new ArrayBuffer(len)` before returning.
- **tsc reference to old `QUALITY_RATE_USD_PER_SECOND` const after rename** — failed because: cost preview JSX still referenced the old name. Replaced with `COST_RATE_USD_PER_SECOND[provider][quality]` matching the new provider-aware shape.
- **bash `cd webapp && ...` after Director switched cwd** — failed because: working dir already inside webapp. Used absolute path `/c/SandyStudio/.claude/worktrees/quizzical-brown-462555/webapp` going forward.

